  /** Target device id (iOS UDID, Android serial, or Chromium id) whose transport session to stop */
  udid: string,
}): Promise<unknown>"},{"path":"tools.argent.rotate","description":"Set the device orientation.
Use when testing layout in a different orientation. Re-run `describe` afterwards: frame coordinates change with the orientation.
On an unfolded foldable iOS simulator (the iPhone Duo), the value sets the orientation of the device, not of the UI: `Portrait` gives a landscape UI and `LandscapeLeft` gives a portrait UI. To fold or unfold the device, use `fold`.
Returns { orientation }. Fails on a TV target, or if the target device is not booted.","signature":"tools.argent.rotate({
  /** Target device id from `list-devices` (iOS UDID or Android serial). */
  udid: string,
  /** Target orientation */
  orientation: "Portrait" | "LandscapeLeft" | "LandscapeRight" | "PortraitUpsideDown",
}): Promise<unknown>"},{"path":"tools.argent.shake","description":"Send a shake gesture to the device (iOS simulator or Android emulator).
Use when you need to trigger anything bound to the shake gesture: iOS's "Undo Typing" / "Redo Typing" prompt in a text field, React Native's developer menu in a debug build, or an app's own shake-to-report handler.
iOS delivers one discrete shake per gesture (the same motion event a physical device raises). Android has no OS-level shake event: the accelerometer is driven through a burst of hard direction changes so app-side detectors fire, and the resting orientation is restored afterwards.
Returns { shaken: true, count }.
Works on local and remote (sim-remote) iOS simulators. Fails on a physical device or a TV: only phone/tablet simulators and emulators are supported.","signature":"tools.argent.shake({
  /** Target device id from `list-devices` (iOS simulator UDID or Android emulator serial). @minLength 1 */
  udid: string,
  /**
   * How many shake gestures to deliver back-to-back (default 1). Raise it for apps whose shake detector needs sustained motion before it fires. Range: 1 to 10.
   * @integer @minimum 1 @maximum 10
   */
  count?: number,
}): Promise<unknown>"}],"remaining":60,"next":{"offset":10}}

